          <h2>始まり</h2>
          <p>
            Ilha Grande (BRAZIL-PI). </br>
            A tiny city cursed by a lack of infrastructure.<br/>
            People around me always saw me as a little genius, 
            and do you know what's a little genius biggest weakness? <br/>
            <p>Ego</p>
          </p>
          <p>
            In my 14s, I fell in love with the Japanese language and 
            fed the audacious dream of enrolling to an exchange program and graduating in Japan.
            I studied obstinately, preparing for the future I was designing myself.
          </p>
        <p></p>
          <h2>
            「はぁ？！
            <br/>日本に交換留学で行きたいの？
            <br/>数学オリンピックが勝ったわけじゃないよ！
            <br/>バーハハハ！」
          </h2>
          <p>
            In a call to the consulate, my dream was shattered.
            That woman's laugh mocked my dream. After all, how 
            could an ordinary boy from Piauí, from a tiny little town, 
            who "never won at a math olympiad" get approved on Monbukagasho? 
          </p>
          <p>
            Those laughs buried the shreds of my remaining dream.
            For years, I put away my Japanese skills and walked away.
            I was pushed into the darkness, seeing my plans turned into a ruin of rubble.
          </p>
        </article>
